From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 14:47:14 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] vulkan: link CoreGraphics for the Metal WSI

wsi_common_metal_layer.m calls CGColorSpaceCreateWithName and
CGColorSpaceRelease and reads the kCGColorSpace* names. On macOS a
framework KosmicKrisp links already brings CoreGraphics in; on iOS
nothing does, and because libvulkan_kosmickrisp links with
-undefined dynamic_lookup the missing symbols would surface only when
dyld loads the driver. Name the framework.

Class: ios-port
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-09-26-kosmickrisp-ios-build.md
Offered-upstream: no
---
 src/vulkan/meson.build | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/vulkan/meson.build b/src/vulkan/meson.build
index 614a33a..261babc 100644
--- a/src/vulkan/meson.build
+++ b/src/vulkan/meson.build
@@ -73,7 +73,7 @@ if with_platform_macos
   vulkan_wsi_list += '-DVK_USE_PLATFORM_METAL_EXT'
   vulkan_wsi_deps += dependency(
     'appleframeworks',
-    modules : ['QuartzCore', 'Metal']
+    modules : ['QuartzCore', 'Metal', 'CoreGraphics']
   )
 endif
 
